{
	title: 'Local notices: toasts for other tabs, push only when nobody watches',
	spec: "A client tells the host which tab it shows while watched: a browser tab while visible and focused; a terminal while its window has focus (it enables terminal focus reporting, CSI ?1004h); a terminal that never reports focus counts as watching whenever it shows a tab. For each event that pushes (turn completed, turn failed, question waiting): if any client watches that session nothing is sent, since the user already sees it; else if any client watches another tab, each such client gets a notice and no push is sent; else a web push as task m1. A notice shows tab number, name, what happened (done, failed, needs your attention) and one line (the reply's last line, the error, or the question). Clients show notices in a stack at the bottom right, just above the tabs: a bar in the event's colour (done green, failed red, attention amber), newest at the bottom, each gone after 5 s, beyond three the oldest fold into '+N more (tab numbers)'; full width on narrow terminals; on the web square cards, a tap opens the tab. The tab's attention mark stays until the tab is visited. No bell (a plugin can add one from the same event). The stack takes entries from any source, and an entry may stay until its source removes it, so later sources (changed files) fit. In the terminal a thin rule (▁) in the notice text colour tops the stack, so its edge shows even when the notice text is short.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Routing lives in src/host/notify.ts (host.broadcast calls notify.route); the stack in src/common/notices.ts (state, timer, fold), drawn by client/notice-view.ts over the rows above the terminal tab bar (modalView.overlay; a short frame grows at the top) and by web/components/Notices.tsx, a zero-height anchor before the StatusRow with the cards absolutely positioned above it (the web tab strip is at the top, so 'above the tabs' means above the status row there).",
		"The notice event names its session in 'session', not 'sessionId': both clients route any event with a sessionId to that session's (hidden) tab and would swallow it.",
		"host.ts used to accept 'visibility' only for a session already in client.open, but open is async (history.open) while visibility arrives right after it, so a freshly shown tab never counted as watched; the check is gone (close still clears it).",
		"Terminal: CSI ?1004h is enabled with bracketed paste; keys.ts decodes CSI I / CSI O into 'focus-in'/'focus-out' keys, which app.onKeys consumes before anything else. tabSwitch.watch sends visibility only on change and forgets on reconnect. The reply's last line comes from the last assistant text record of the latest turn (pages.page), not from stream events."
	],
	needs: ['m1']
}
